From: Sukrit Jaidee <45908411+SukritJaAIproject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:09:07 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] build(desktop): Windows desktop packaging for iMPS Fault
 Detection

Electron shell (desktop/electron/main.cjs) that starts a PyInstaller one-folder
Python sidecar and the production Next.js standalone server on random loopback
ports, waits for runtime health (180 s first-run budget for EDR scans), then
opens the dashboard; --smoke-test runs the same path headless. The sidecar is
NumPy-only inference (LSTM-AE / GRU converted from the trained weights, no
PyTorch) plus a job worker, bundled Wireshark/TShark 4.4.6 with dsV2Gshark
1.5.1 and app-local VC++ runtime DLLs, so a target machine needs no Node,
Python, Wireshark, Npcap or MongoDB. desktop/scripts prepare the bundle and
build NSIS installers in two flavours - Offline (self-contained) and Online
(small bootstrapper that downloads a SHA-512-checked .nsis.7z payload) - with a
release manifest and SHA256SUMS. desktop/README.md is the build/install runbook;
desktop/licenses holds the third-party notices.

package.json: version 1.2.0, electron-builder config, desktop:* scripts,
electron 44.3.0 / electron-builder 26.15.3. next.config.js emits a standalone
build into .next-desktop when IMPS_DESKTOP_BUILD=1. .gitignore covers the
desktop build outputs plus the scratch/hand-off directories (output/, tmp/).

Implemented with Codex 2026-09-17..22 and committed from the working tree as
handed over. Known gaps are documented in desktop/README.md: installers are
unsigned, and the Online payload URLs are not published yet.

